{"type": "spr", "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The base of a right rectangular pyramid has a length of <math alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn>\n</math> centimeters and a width of <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math> centimeters. The height of this pyramid is <math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math> centimeters. What is the volume, in cubic centimeters, of this pyramid?</p>", "keys": ["126"], "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"126\"><mn>126</mn></math>. It&rsquo;s given that the base of the right rectangular pyramid has a length of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn></math> centimeters and a width of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn></math> centimeters and that the height of the pyramid is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn></math> centimeters. The volume, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V\"><mi>V</mi></math>, of a right rectangular pyramid is given by the formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V equals one third script l w h\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>h</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi></math> are the length and width, respectively, of the pyramid&rsquo;s base and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi></math> is the height of the pyramid. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi></math> in this formula yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V equals one third left parenthesis 27 right parenthesis left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis left parenthesis 7 right parenthesis\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>(</mo><mn>27</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V equals 126\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>126</mn></math>. Therefore, the volume, in cubic centimeters, of the pyramid is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"126\"><mn>126</mn></math>.</p>", "externalid": "86cc8eb8-5cbf-4188-9abd-1839bfec0526", "correct_answer": ["126"]}